/* Folder badges — FROSTED-GLASS LOZENGES hung on the diorama.
   Redesign (2026-07): the old "SNES 3D item tag" (a 4-colour hard bevel + a
   `0 2px 0` block drop) read as a pasted game button floating ON the painted
   meadow — the two tells of the "not blended" look. This reworks each chip into
   a frosted-glass CAPSULE that lets the scene blur THROUGH it (blend) while a
   substantial cream frost + a white ink scrim keep the label crisp over the
   busy field (readability). It adopts the bar frame's "gallery-hung painting"
   language: ONE warm hairline (no bevel), soft feathered elevation (no hard
   drop), and a glass-edge inner top highlight. Design research: frosted glass
   needs MORE blur over intricate backgrounds (NN/g); a near-solid protected
   panel + a light text-shadow scrim give per-letter figure-ground separation
   over a busy field (badgezoo / Smashing); an inner light edge is what makes it
   read as real glass (Comeau). The capsule shape also correctly signals a
   TAG/identity chip, distinct from the rounded-rect control buttons. */
[data-theme="tofu"] .folder-badge{
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(252,250,245,0.72) 0%, rgba(244,240,231,0.6) 100%);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(10px) saturate(1.35);
  backdrop-filter:blur(10px) saturate(1.35);
  color:#5A4A32;
  border:1px solid rgba(140,116,80,0.3);
  border-radius:999px;
  padding:3px 12px;
  box-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(74,58,36,0.10),
    0 4px 10px -5px rgba(96,76,48,0.22),
    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.65);
  text-shadow:0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.5);
  font-weight:700;
  transition:transform 0.16s cubic-bezier(0.22,0.9,0.3,1.1), box-shadow 0.16s ease, background 0.16s ease
}
[data-theme="tofu"] .folder-badge:hover{
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.82) 0%, rgba(250,246,238,0.7) 100%);
  border-color:rgba(140,116,80,0.45);
  color:#4A3820;
  transform:translateY(-1px);
  box-shadow:
    0 2px 4px rgba(74,58,36,0.12),
    0 8px 18px -6px rgba(96,76,48,0.28),
    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.75)
}
[data-theme="tofu"] .folder-badge:active{
  transform:translateY(0);
  box-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(74,58,36,0.12),
    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.6)
}
/* Read-only root — a cooler, de-saturated frost + the lock glyph, so "locked"
   reads distinctly from a writable chip while staying the SAME glass material.
   Own selector at (0,3,0) so it wins over the writable tofu chip regardless of
   source order. */
[data-theme="tofu"] .folder-badge.folder-badge-ro{
  background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(238,238,236,0.66) 0%, rgba(226,226,224,0.56) 100%);
