  border-width:4px;
  box-shadow:var(--clay-sm)}
/* :not(.memory-modal) — the memory modal owns a complete --m-* design system
   and must not inherit the generic tofu input styling. Excluding it here at the
   SOURCE (specificity 0,3,1) lets its own .memory-modal .memory-* rules win by
   normal cascade in every theme, retiring ~15 counter-!important overrides that
   previously existed only to beat this over-broad bleed.
   :not(.recent-search-input) — SAME source-exclusion pattern: the project
   modal's Recent-search box owns its own blocky tofu styling
   ([data-theme="tofu"] .recent-search .recent-search-input, specificity 0,3,0).
   Without this carve-out this bleed (0,3,1) out-specifies it and flattens its
   intended 2px ink border to the generic 1px — so exclude it at the source
   rather than adding an !important counter-rule. Proven by
   tests/test_recent_search_tofu_specificity.py. */
[data-theme="tofu"] .modal:not(.memory-modal) input:not(.recent-search-input){
  border-radius:var(--radius);
