/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   INPUT — Warm Reading Room composer
   A calm paper box: soft border, diffuse shadow, quiet focus
   ring. No controller frame, pet mascot, sparkles, D-pad or
   speech-bubble tail — all decorative pseudo-elements retired.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-area{
  background:transparent;
  border-top:none;
  box-shadow:none;
  position:relative;
  padding-top:8px
}
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-box{
  /* Item 1 — adopt the project bar's "gallery-hung frame" vocabulary: one slim
     warm frame line + soft two-layer elevation (a tight contact shadow + a
     feathered ambient halo), 14px radius. Kinship with .project-bar (styles.css
     :11931), NOT a re-added game panel. STATIC — no animation on the box. */
  border:1.5px solid rgba(140,116,80,0.34);
  background:#FFFDF9;
  border-radius:14px;
  box-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(74,58,36,0.10),
    0 8px 22px -8px rgba(96,76,48,0.22);
  isolation:auto;
  overflow:visible;
  transition:border-color 0.2s ease,box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  position:relative;
  z-index:2
}
/* Decorative pseudo-elements retired (pet mascot / grip wings) */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-box::before,
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-box::after{
  content:none;
  display:none
}
/* Decorative pseudo-elements retired (sparkles) */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-area::before,
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-area::after{
  content:none;
  display:none
}
/* Decorative pseudo-elements retired (D-pad / button dots) */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-row::before,
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-row::after{
  content:none;
  display:none
}
/* Decorative pseudo-element retired (speech-bubble tail) */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-inner::before{
  content:none;
  display:none
}
/* ── Focus state: quiet accent ring, no lift ── */
[data-theme="tofu"] .input-box:focus-within{
  /* Item 3 — warm focus echoing the bar's hover-warmth: deepen the warm frame,
     widen the ambient shadow a touch, and add a soft warm-amber ring (the bar's
     #C4956A family). NO lift, NO animation; the glow lives on the box FRAME
     (box-shadow OUTSIDE the border) — never a layer behind the live text. */
  border-color:rgba(140,116,80,0.62);
  box-shadow:
    0 1px 2px rgba(74,58,36,0.10),
    0 10px 26px -8px rgba(96,76,48,0.28),
    0 0 0 3px rgba(196,149,106,0.22);
  transform:none
}
/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Item 4 — SCENE-TINTED WASH behind the input TOOLBAR TRAY ONLY.
   The input box "follows suit" with the project bar by echoing the SAME scene
   the bar shows: .project-bar carries [data-decor] (set by tofu-pet.js) and is
   a SIBLING of .input-box inside .input-inner, so a pure-CSS general-sibling
   selector reads the decor at runtime with NO JS / NO bundle change (it even
   updates live when the scene is cycled).

   HARD CONSTRAINTS (owner, non-negotiable):
   • STATIC only — no canvas, no pet, no critter, no animation.
   • Behind the TOOLBAR TRAY (.input-actions) ONLY — the wash is a `background`
     on the tray element, a SEPARATE child from .input-row/textarea, so it can
     NEVER sit behind the live typing surface.
   • VERY low saturation (near-white scene tints, same family as the bar body
     wash) so pill labels + placeholder contrast hold.
   • NO new position/z-index (a background paints behind the tray's own children
     automatically) → cannot trap #imagePreviews / overlays into flow.
   • Desktop-only (min-width:769px) so the mobile compact toolbar stays byte-
     identical (mobile strips decorations by design).
   • Gated to a VISIBLE, scened bar: :not([style*="none"]) (the bar is
     display:none when no project) and excludes [data-decor="off"].
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
@media(min-width:769px){
  /* Tray shape — hug the 14px gallery frame instead of a hard rectangle, and a
     soft recessed "lip" (inset top highlight) so the toolbar reads as a panel
     set INTO the box, not a solid block pasted under it. Static, no motion,
     tray-only; desktop-only keeps the mobile compact toolbar byte-identical. */
  [data-theme="tofu"] .input-box .input-actions{
    border-radius:0 0 12.5px 12.5px;
    box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.55)
  }
  /* ATMOSPHERIC WATERCOLOR WASH — mirrors HOW the bar's <canvas> Impressionist
     scene actually reads (tofu-scene.js PALETTES): a LIGHT top band (so the
     frosted pill labels keep contrast — the bar keeps its upper band pale for
     the same reason) with the scene's saturated colour POOLED LOW, plus two
     LARGE, SOFT, NON-TILED complementary blooms (the bar's "broken colour"
     flecks: poppy in the meadow greens, lavender-lily in the pool teals, peach
     in the dawn sky). NON-tiled = full-cover soft gradients (no background-size
     repeat) → watercolour atmosphere, NOT the polka-dot texture a tiled dab
     field produced. STATIC — pure layered CSS gradients (no canvas/pet/critter/
     animation). Blooms sit low + stay low-alpha, and the frosted pills blur
     them further, so pill labels + placeholder contrast hold. Colours are drawn
     straight from the bar's per-scene gradient + fleck palette so the input
     genuinely echoes the SAME painting the bar shows. */
  [data-theme="tofu"] .project-bar[data-decor="meadow"]:not([style*="none"]) ~ .input-box .input-actions{
    background:
      radial-gradient(135% 108% at 20% 138%, rgba(124,164,87,0.30) 0%, rgba(124,164,87,0) 64%),
      radial-gradient(95% 90% at 86% 130%, rgba(224,114,138,0.13) 0%, rgba(224,114,138,0) 60%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(238,243,226,0) 0%, rgba(224,237,208,0.5) 56%, rgba(188,210,140,0.56) 100%)
  }
  [data-theme="tofu"] .project-bar[data-decor="pool"]:not([style*="none"]) ~ .input-box .input-actions{
